On my side, I made the wand-bag-mistake two (maybe three) times in my life.
Now I'm cured and it didn't happen for many years.  Because I know that
it's fatal(*) I am very cautious.  I put wands of cancellation visible in
the first inventory slots starting with c, and whenever I put in new items
I check the selected items again before confirming.

More often, OTOH, I forget in a combat to check after every hit/curse whether
I am ok or not.  I think the reason is that a combat is a longer sequence of
moves as opposed to a bag action that happens just in one move where I can be
cautious.

Apparently other players are used to be more cautious during combat, which
is a Fine Thing.

(*) Not quite true... it may not be fatal, but makes things a lot harder.
Had once my bag been eaten by some creature at Molochs Sanctum.  Ascended
that unfortunate character nevertheless.

